Use module-scoped verification names, dependency heights and builtin inventories
in the default translator. Unrelated module growth no longer changes another
unit's translated text. This intentionally changes generated Boogie once and can
move solver resource costs. Translation-table consumers use the same graph
materialization and module-owned proof/report maps as uncached consumers.

The moved Base64 encoding proof checks its existing obligations in separate assertion batches, within its unchanged resource limit.

The moved structural-JSON function checks its existing well-formedness obligations separately, within its unchanged resource limit.

The original well-founded induction regression and the one-padding Base64 decomposition lemma keep their existing proof obligations and resource ceilings, with assertion isolation to repair moved proof costs. Generated-name and canonical builtin-display expectations follow the new ownership scheme.
